WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:03:08.970
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
03:09.240 --> 03:13.600
Grandpa, thank you so much for saving Grandma.

3
03:13.680 --> 03:15.320
The person you should thank is over there.

4
03:15.400 --> 03:16.600
‎PREVIOUSLY

5
03:16.680 --> 03:19.040
He asked me to come help you.

6
03:19.960 --> 03:21.320
Hathaya is staying here.

7
03:22.200 --> 03:24.560
I brought Hathaya back to help with the development.

8
03:24.640 --> 03:26.480
Papang's not at home.

9
03:26.560 --> 03:29.120
I'm afraid he may have run away like he threatened to before.

10
03:29.200 --> 03:32.600
You're his father. Don't you feel anything at all?

11
03:36.000 --> 03:36.880
Yes, ma'am.

12
03:38.680 --> 03:40.080
Any luck finding Papang?

13
03:40.160 --> 03:43.200
Not yet. I sent Papang's picture to the development's chat group

14
03:43.280 --> 03:45.440
so security and residents can look for him.

15
03:45.520 --> 03:47.080
Have you told Ramil yet?

16
03:47.160 --> 03:48.080
I called him already.

17
03:48.920 --> 03:50.400
Then you go join Ramil.

18
03:50.480 --> 03:52.280
I'll ask around at the shops near the entrance.

19
03:52.360 --> 03:53.640
Okay.

20
04:00.360 --> 04:01.200
Any luck?

21
04:01.760 --> 04:04.080
Nothing. We looked everywhere, but no luck.

22
04:04.160 --> 04:07.320
Are you sure Papang isn't hiding in the house like last time?

23
04:07.400 --> 04:08.840
I searched everywhere.

24
04:10.800 --> 04:12.040
Why would Papang run away?

25
04:16.040 --> 04:18.040
I asked at the shops near the entrance.

26
04:18.120 --> 04:20.839
They said they saw Papang running toward the main road.

27
04:22.240 --> 04:25.760
And they also said there's a child-abduction gang.

28
04:25.840 --> 04:28.160
A few days ago, they kidnapped a child,

29
04:28.240 --> 04:30.640
and the police still haven't caught them.

30
04:31.720 --> 04:33.000
A child-abduction gang?

31
04:39.840 --> 04:41.440
Get in.

32
04:43.000 --> 04:44.280
Should we go back?

33
04:45.880 --> 04:48.280
Let's not waste the trip. Drive around one more time.

34
04:50.320 --> 04:51.960
Go. Drive.

35
04:56.320 --> 04:58.200
Where did Sanguansri go?

36
04:59.640 --> 05:02.480
I asked where your madam went.

37
05:05.320 --> 05:09.240
Papang ran away from home, Dad. She went to help look for him.

38
05:09.320 --> 05:11.680
Does no one in this house understand a simple order?

39
05:11.760 --> 05:14.480
I told her not to get involved with that family.

40
05:15.680 --> 05:18.160
She can deal with me when she gets back.

41
05:19.640 --> 05:20.480
Dad.

42
05:22.520 --> 05:24.080
I'm going out to help look for Papang.

43
05:25.480 --> 05:28.120
What is wrong with everyone in this house?

44
05:28.640 --> 05:30.880
Are you going to disobey me too?

45
05:38.320 --> 05:39.840
I'm sorry, Dad,

46
05:40.640 --> 05:42.160
but I have to help look for Papang.

47
05:43.720 --> 05:46.000
You dare disobey me, Raiwin?

48
05:46.080 --> 05:47.640
If Ramil finds out

49
05:47.720 --> 05:50.200
that Papang ran away because of the lies you told him,

50
05:50.280 --> 05:51.640
he won't let this go.

51
05:51.720 --> 05:53.960
And what exactly can he do to me?

52
05:58.800 --> 06:01.200
-Serve the rice. -Yes, sir.

53
06:01.840 --> 06:03.920
Your madam isn't here, so you forgot how to work?

54
06:05.640 --> 06:07.440
Dad, you taught me

55
06:07.520 --> 06:09.440
that a politician needs a good public image.

56
06:10.080 --> 06:11.440
A reliable community figure.

57
06:11.520 --> 06:15.160
That's exactly the image I'm building right now.

58
06:17.000 --> 06:18.760
Raiwin, get back here.

59
06:19.960 --> 06:21.120
Dammit!

60
06:21.800 --> 06:25.240
Damn that kid. All he does is cause trouble.

61
06:25.320 --> 06:27.200
Would you like your rice now, sir?

62
06:27.280 --> 06:28.960
No! Get out.

63
06:29.040 --> 06:30.800
I don't want to look at you.

64
06:31.560 --> 06:34.440
That damn kid. It'd be better if he died.

65
06:35.880 --> 06:37.520
There'd be one less problem to deal with.

66
06:56.240 --> 06:57.760
Mommy.

67
06:58.640 --> 07:01.280
Which way is Mommy's house?

68
07:07.080 --> 07:11.080
Mommy. I'm hungry.

69
07:27.880 --> 07:29.800
Someone said they saw Papang.

70
07:29.880 --> 07:32.200
Are they sure it wasn't another child?

71
07:33.160 --> 07:35.440
I showed them his picture. They're sure it was him.

72
07:35.520 --> 07:38.160
They said he was wearing these exact clothes.

73
07:39.160 --> 07:40.480
This is my fault.

74
07:40.560 --> 07:44.360
I made him think I was abandoning him. If anything happens to Papang,

75
07:44.440 --> 07:45.600
I'll never forgive myself.

76
07:46.800 --> 07:49.480
I'm sure Papang is safe. Let's go find him.

77
07:50.080 --> 07:51.000
Come on.

78
07:54.960 --> 07:58.040
Any news, Officer? Have you found my grandson?

79
07:59.000 --> 08:01.160
Please keep looking for him.

80
08:04.920 --> 08:08.240
Auntie. Let's go look for Papang.

81
08:11.640 --> 08:12.600
Yes.

82
08:16.120 --> 08:17.360
Daddy.

83
08:18.600 --> 08:20.360
Where are you?

84
08:21.280 --> 08:23.400
I miss you, Daddy.

85
08:24.800 --> 08:27.240
Please come help me, Daddy.

86
08:35.919 --> 08:38.360
Daddy came to get me.

87
08:38.440 --> 08:40.080
Daddy.

88
08:53.000 --> 08:56.000
Hey, little guy. Where are you going?

89
08:56.080 --> 08:57.040
Why are you walking around out here by yourself?

90
08:57.120 --> 08:59.240
I'm trying to find Mommy,

91
08:59.320 --> 09:01.520
but I don't remember the way home.

92
09:01.600 --> 09:03.440
I want to go back to Daddy.

93
09:03.520 --> 09:06.560
And where does your dad live?

94
09:08.400 --> 09:10.800
Over there. There's a fountain at the roundabout.

95
09:12.760 --> 09:15.200
Oh, the fountain roundabout. I know where that is.

96
09:15.280 --> 09:18.560
I'm going that way anyway. Want me to give you a ride home?

97
09:20.240 --> 09:22.760
Okay? It's dark and deserted.

98
09:22.840 --> 09:24.840
Your dad must be really worried.

99
09:24.920 --> 09:27.160
Come with me. I'll take you all the way home.

100
09:27.240 --> 09:28.560
Play with toys.

101
09:29.400 --> 09:30.680
Come on. Get in.

102
09:34.480 --> 09:36.800
Come on. Get in.

103
09:36.880 --> 09:38.960
Hop in. There are other kids in here.

104
09:39.480 --> 09:42.480
You can sit together and play. It'll be fun. Come on.

105
09:43.440 --> 09:45.800
I told you to get in.

106
09:45.880 --> 09:46.880
Do we have to force you?

107
09:52.000 --> 09:54.360
-Go get him. Quickly. -Help!

108
09:55.000 --> 09:58.400
Help. Help!

109
10:00.040 --> 10:00.880
That's it.

110
10:00.960 --> 10:04.360
You're just going to tire yourself out. Go wait in the AC van.

111
10:04.440 --> 10:06.320
-Grab him. -Wait.

112
10:06.400 --> 10:10.360
Sit down. Just sit there and look cool. I'll handle this kid myself.

113
10:10.440 --> 10:13.360
I'm still mad about that kick he gave me.

114
10:16.400 --> 10:17.320
Hey!

115
10:17.400 --> 10:19.720
-Let me go. Help. -Come here. Quiet.

116
10:19.800 --> 10:20.800
-Somebody help me. -Come on.

117
10:22.240 --> 10:24.480
-Quiet. Shut up. -Somebody help me.

118
10:24.560 --> 10:27.200
-Daddy's here. Daddy. -Let go of my son.

119
10:27.880 --> 10:29.160
Take care of the kid.

120
10:29.240 --> 10:31.440
Wait. I'll handle him myself.

121
10:39.560 --> 10:42.320
That was luck.

122
10:42.400 --> 10:43.840
This time I'm serious.

123
10:46.160 --> 10:47.320
I'm serious.

124
10:56.680 --> 10:59.440
Quit sitting there like an idiot. Come help me.

125
10:59.520 --> 11:02.440
-Hurry up. -Papang.

126
11:10.680 --> 11:13.200
-Papang. -Get in. Don't fight.

127
11:19.280 --> 11:20.160
Come here.

128
11:21.040 --> 11:22.520
Hit him. He can take it.

129
11:24.560 --> 11:26.840
See? Doesn't even hurt him.

130
11:36.480 --> 11:37.880
Hey. You said it doesn't hurt.

131
11:40.640 --> 11:42.600
Wake up. Get up.

132
11:46.400 --> 11:48.560
Auntie, watch out.

133
11:49.120 --> 11:50.080
Stay behind me.

134
11:51.360 --> 11:52.520
You really wanna die, huh?

135
11:52.600 --> 11:54.800
Hathaya, get back.

136
12:05.720 --> 12:07.080
Stop right there.

137
12:07.880 --> 12:09.320
You think you're tough?

138
12:09.400 --> 12:10.680
Time to pay you back.

139
12:22.240 --> 12:24.320
What was that?

140
12:31.280 --> 12:34.520
That was only a warning shot. This time, I'll shoot for real.

141
12:35.040 --> 12:37.680
Don't try anything. Drop your weapons. The police are on their way.

142
12:37.760 --> 12:39.040
Police?

143
13:14.240 --> 13:16.000
Ms. Sanguansri called.

144
13:16.080 --> 13:18.080
They found Papang.

145
13:18.160 --> 13:20.880
Everyone is at the police station now, and they'll be coming back soon.

146
13:25.240 --> 13:26.360
Come with me.

147
13:43.000 --> 13:44.880
We're home.

148
13:44.960 --> 13:46.680
Let me get the door for you. Just a sec.

149
13:50.120 --> 13:52.200
Come on.

150
13:53.160 --> 13:54.000
Alright.

151
13:54.880 --> 13:56.960
We're home.

152
13:58.720 --> 14:00.040
Daddy, what happened to you?

153
14:04.800 --> 14:08.040
As long as you're safe, Daddy doesn't hurt anymore.

154
14:19.280 --> 14:20.840
And Grandma

155
14:21.640 --> 14:23.280
was worried about you too.

156
14:32.640 --> 14:36.400
You're safe now, sweetheart. Don't ever do something like this again, okay?

157
14:44.240 --> 14:45.400
Papang.

158
14:46.360 --> 14:49.600
I told you not to run away from home.

159
14:50.480 --> 14:51.840
Why did you do it?

160
14:52.480 --> 14:54.960
I thought Daddy was gone.

161
14:55.040 --> 14:56.800
I thought nobody loved me.

162
14:56.880 --> 14:58.920
Why would you think that?

163
14:59.000 --> 15:01.240
-Because-- -Ramil.

164
15:03.360 --> 15:04.680
Can I talk to Papang for a minute?

165
15:06.400 --> 15:09.560
You must be hungry. Daddy will go make you something to eat.

166
15:16.000 --> 15:17.160
Then I'll head home now.

167
15:29.040 --> 15:30.240
Papang.

168
15:31.440 --> 15:34.040
Papang, I know you ran away

169
15:34.120 --> 15:36.760
because you were hurt by the mean things Grandpa said to you.

170
15:37.840 --> 15:40.560
Your father doesn't want to take care of you.

171
15:40.640 --> 15:42.560
Everyone hates you.

172
15:42.640 --> 15:46.800
No one loves you. Everyone here hates you.

173
15:47.400 --> 15:49.160
Grandpa didn't mean it.

174
15:50.560 --> 15:53.640
He was arguing with Ramil

175
15:53.720 --> 15:57.200
and was upset. He took that anger out on you.

176
15:57.280 --> 15:59.640
Then why did Grandpa say those things?

177
16:00.400 --> 16:02.040
He didn't mean them.

178
16:02.120 --> 16:05.280
When Grandpa heard that you ran away,

179
16:05.880 --> 16:08.840
he got worried. That's why he told me

180
16:08.920 --> 16:10.720
to come look for you.

181
16:10.800 --> 16:12.320
Papang.

182
16:12.400 --> 16:15.480
If you don't want Grandpa and Daddy to fight again,

183
16:16.960 --> 16:18.720
could you not tell Daddy what Grandpa said?

184
16:22.480 --> 16:24.920
Okay. I won't tell Daddy.

185
16:27.320 --> 16:28.880
That's my good…

186
16:32.600 --> 16:33.520
nephew.

187
16:34.920 --> 16:37.400
Thank you for helping me, Uncle.

188
16:38.840 --> 16:39.880
Go inside.

189
17:04.480 --> 17:06.599
-Let's eat. -Okay.

190
17:07.560 --> 17:11.680
You still haven't answered me.

191
17:11.760 --> 17:14.760
Why did you run away?

192
17:15.599 --> 17:18.400
I woke up and couldn't find you.

193
17:18.480 --> 17:21.280
I thought you left me.

194
17:24.000 --> 17:25.560
Papang.

195
17:25.640 --> 17:29.200
Remember this. Daddy loves you more than anything.

196
17:30.160 --> 17:33.200
Promise me

197
17:33.280 --> 17:34.880
that you'll never do this again.

198
17:34.960 --> 17:37.600
I'm sorry. I promise.

199
17:37.680 --> 17:39.800
Good. You promised.

200
17:39.880 --> 17:42.200
Don't do this again,

201
17:42.280 --> 17:43.560
-okay? -Okay.

202
17:43.640 --> 17:44.800
Let's eat then.

203
17:45.440 --> 17:46.880
Eat plenty of vegetables.

204
17:46.960 --> 17:48.960
Get some vegetables.

205
17:50.960 --> 17:52.920
Eat some vegetables. Let me see you eat some.

206
17:55.040 --> 17:57.120
Very good.

207
18:00.520 --> 18:03.480
Where are my clothes? Did you pack up my things?

208
18:10.200 --> 18:12.800
You dared disobey me?

209
18:12.880 --> 18:14.800
If you don't want to live here, then leave.

210
18:14.880 --> 18:18.000
Go live with your son. Go live with your grandson.

211
18:22.840 --> 18:24.040
Put this back in my room.

212
18:27.480 --> 18:28.680
Go.

213
18:31.800 --> 18:33.640
You've gotten pretty bold, Sanguansri.

214
18:33.720 --> 18:35.880
If you aren't afraid of starving, why live off me?

215
18:35.960 --> 18:39.080
I wasn't trying to defy you.

216
18:39.160 --> 18:42.440
Don't make excuses. Then why did you go looking for that damn kid?

217
18:42.520 --> 18:44.960
I went to help find my grandson

218
18:45.040 --> 18:46.680
to keep Ramil from blaming you.

219
18:46.760 --> 18:48.680
You lied to Papang and upset him

220
18:48.760 --> 18:50.840
so badly that he ran away.

221
18:50.920 --> 18:53.560
You think I'm afraid of Ramil? He should be afraid of me.

222
18:53.640 --> 18:55.840
I supported you and those people for decades.

223
18:55.920 --> 18:59.080
You've been living off me all this time.

224
18:59.680 --> 19:03.000
I've been with you for more than 20 years.

225
19:03.560 --> 19:04.800
Was all I did for nothing?

226
19:07.600 --> 19:10.400
If that's all my love and concern are worth to you,

227
19:11.040 --> 19:12.160
then now I know my place.

228
19:14.280 --> 19:16.880
I'm nothing more than a servant

229
19:17.880 --> 19:19.840
who works just for food and shelter.

230
19:20.440 --> 19:22.360
And the reason I disobeyed you

231
19:23.000 --> 19:25.080
was because I wanted to help Papang.

232
19:26.120 --> 19:28.840
You may hate him and refuse to accept him,

233
19:28.920 --> 19:31.840
but you still can't deny that he's your own blood.

234
19:39.960 --> 19:41.360
Go upstairs and get some rest.

235
19:42.640 --> 19:45.040
You too. You're going over my head now?

236
19:46.560 --> 19:48.480
I love you, and I'm worried about you, Dad.

237
19:49.040 --> 19:51.200
That's why I went to help look for Papang.

238
19:51.280 --> 19:53.080
And I asked him

239
19:53.160 --> 19:56.680
not to tell anyone that you were the reason he ran away.

240
19:56.760 --> 19:59.040
Are you insulting me?

241
19:59.120 --> 20:01.040
That's not what I mean.

242
20:01.120 --> 20:03.400
But if the kidnapping gang had taken Papang

243
20:03.480 --> 20:06.440
and something terrible had happened, everyone would have blamed you.

244
20:08.160 --> 20:10.680
Are you threatening me, Raiwin?

245
20:11.360 --> 20:12.920
No one is threatening you.

246
20:13.000 --> 20:14.960
Everyone is trying to protect you.

247
20:20.560 --> 20:22.440
Why are you interfering in my family?

248
20:23.040 --> 20:25.760
You're an outsider. Get out.

249
20:26.360 --> 20:29.520
If you weren't the reason Papang ran away,

250
20:29.600 --> 20:31.240
I wouldn't have set foot in here.

251
20:32.280 --> 20:35.160
You're an adult with a respectable job.

252
20:35.240 --> 20:37.400
You should feel bad for what you did,

253
20:37.480 --> 20:41.040
yet you hurt a child who just needs kindness

254
20:41.120 --> 20:44.680
and love. If you can't show him kindness

255
20:44.760 --> 20:46.440
or compassion,

256
20:46.520 --> 20:49.880
then leave him alone. You have no right to destroy his feelings like that.

257
20:49.960 --> 20:51.560
Who do you think you are?

258
20:52.080 --> 20:54.720
What gives you the right to lecture me in my own house? Get out.

259
20:54.800 --> 20:56.320
I will.

260
20:56.400 --> 20:58.480
But you need to hear me first.

261
20:59.720 --> 21:02.920
This time, I'll turn a blind eye

262
21:03.000 --> 21:04.800
to what you did.

263
21:05.720 --> 21:08.720
But if you ever hurt Papang like this again,

264
21:09.480 --> 21:10.320
I won't let it go.

265
21:11.160 --> 21:13.520
Get out, and don't ever set foot in here again.

266
21:13.600 --> 21:15.760
Do you understand?

267
21:15.840 --> 21:18.040
And don't ever let her into this house again.

268
21:19.960 --> 21:21.160
That goes for both of you.

269
21:22.400 --> 21:23.760
Stay away from that woman.

270
21:26.560 --> 21:27.520
Let's go.

271
21:31.200 --> 21:34.560
You think you can challenge me?

272
21:35.080 --> 21:36.760
You picked the wrong man.

273
21:46.920 --> 21:49.440
Aunt Hathaya finished cooking.

274
21:49.520 --> 21:50.800
Come on. Let's eat.

275
21:54.160 --> 21:57.040
I will get you something to drink. What do you want? Red soda?

276
22:09.320 --> 22:12.240
Auntie knows the secret between you and Uncle Raiwin.

277
22:15.520 --> 22:19.160
You did a very good thing by forgiving Grandpa.

278
22:28.000 --> 22:31.440
You don't love me. Why did you serve me food?

279
22:33.040 --> 22:36.560
Who said I don't love you? And I don't hate you either.

280
22:37.680 --> 22:40.960
Feelings can change.

281
22:41.640 --> 22:44.640
What about you? Do you like me a little now?

282
22:53.440 --> 22:54.400
Stay behind me.

283
22:55.200 --> 22:57.240
Hathaya, get back.

284
23:06.560 --> 23:09.240
-Well? -Are you done talking yet?

285
23:17.560 --> 23:19.360
So we can finally eat.

286
23:22.560 --> 23:25.480
Thank you for helping me.

287
23:29.440 --> 23:30.880
Thank you, Mother…

288
23:33.400 --> 23:35.080
Mother witch.

289
23:37.600 --> 23:38.800
-Little imp. -Witch.

290
23:38.880 --> 23:40.120
-Little imp. -Witch.

291
23:40.200 --> 23:41.440
-Little imp. -Witch.

292
23:41.520 --> 23:44.760
All right, little imp and witch. The wizard has arrived.

293
23:45.720 --> 23:48.840
Finish everything on your plate. If you don't,

294
23:48.920 --> 23:50.520
I'll turn you into a little imp.

295
23:51.120 --> 23:51.960
Little imp.

296
23:53.600 --> 23:54.880
-Witch. -Little imp.

297
23:54.960 --> 23:57.720
-Witch. -Eat first, little imp and witch.

298
23:58.680 --> 24:00.640
Little imp. Witch.

299
24:03.480 --> 24:05.640
-Want some too, witch? -No, thanks.

300
24:09.080 --> 24:11.200
Let's eat.

301
24:17.800 --> 24:19.320
How's your arm?

302
24:20.360 --> 24:22.000
It's okay. It's getting better.

303
24:22.760 --> 24:26.560
Don't forget your medicine, and try not to use that arm too much.

304
24:29.080 --> 24:32.240
Thank you for helping take care of Papang.

305
24:32.320 --> 24:34.080
It's okay.

306
24:34.160 --> 24:37.080
He may be stubborn and may not like me very much,

307
24:37.160 --> 24:40.680
but he's still a child, and I feel sorry for what he's going through.

308
24:42.840 --> 24:44.800
I'll take the best care of him I can,

309
24:44.880 --> 24:47.280
and I'll keep trying to reach Nuchwara so she can come get him.

310
24:48.160 --> 24:49.400
I hope it works out.

311
24:51.000 --> 24:51.880
Thanks.

312
24:57.520 --> 24:59.680
There are a lot of customers looking at houses today.

313
25:00.720 --> 25:02.280
Are you running some special promotion?

314
25:03.800 --> 25:05.040
Not that I know of.

315
25:06.000 --> 25:08.400
I need to go take care of them. See you later.

316
25:18.600 --> 25:20.240
Aren't you going to welcome them?

317
25:20.320 --> 25:22.600
Well…

318
25:23.840 --> 25:25.760
Hello. Hello.

319
25:25.840 --> 25:27.120
Hello. Hello.

320
25:29.760 --> 25:32.520
Hello, Uncle. Are you here to look at a house?

321
25:33.240 --> 25:35.160
I brought some customers.

322
25:35.720 --> 25:36.920
They're all people I know.

323
25:38.120 --> 25:40.000
Thank you so much, Uncle.

324
25:40.720 --> 25:44.520
Why are you thanking me? I didn't bring those customers for you.

325
25:47.760 --> 25:49.080
Please take good care of them.

326
25:53.880 --> 25:57.080
Thank you so much for bringing customers to me, Uncle.

327
25:57.160 --> 25:58.360
You really didn't have to.

328
25:58.440 --> 26:00.320
Don't worry about it, Chayanee.

329
26:00.400 --> 26:04.600
You'll be joining my family soon enough.

330
26:04.680 --> 26:07.360
Anything I promised you,

331
26:07.440 --> 26:09.120
I'll do everything I can to deliver.

332
26:09.200 --> 26:12.640
That way, Mr. Pichai, your grandpa, can be proud

333
26:12.720 --> 26:14.240
of his favorite granddaughter.

334
26:15.040 --> 26:17.400
By the way, I brought

335
26:17.480 --> 26:19.240
the customers all the way here.

336
26:19.320 --> 26:22.280
Do you have any good promotions for my friends?

337
26:23.480 --> 26:26.240
Any customers you recommend are premium customers.

338
26:26.320 --> 26:28.800
I'll give them a special promotion with free air conditioners

339
26:28.880 --> 26:32.320
and kitchen appliances. Plus, if they fail to qualify for financing,

340
26:32.400 --> 26:35.320
I'll refund their reservation deposit in full.

341
26:38.080 --> 26:40.960
That's what I like to hear.

342
26:41.040 --> 26:43.320
A new-generation executive has to be bold.

343
26:43.400 --> 26:47.320
Chaya, you still need to check each customer's income information carefully.

344
26:48.240 --> 26:51.200
Hathaya, you don't need to teach me how to do my job.

345
26:51.960 --> 26:54.520
I've been doing this for a long time, and I've never made a mistake.

346
26:54.600 --> 26:56.240
Why don't you spend your time finding

347
26:56.320 --> 26:58.760
half as many customers as I have?

348
27:04.200 --> 27:06.560
Uncle, please come to the VIP lounge.

349
27:06.640 --> 27:07.480
Right over there.

350
27:18.640 --> 27:20.120
Are you interested?

351
27:20.200 --> 27:22.320
I can recommend some good promotions for you.

352
27:22.840 --> 27:26.480
The house is beautiful, and the promotions are good. I like it. I'll reserve one.

353
27:27.160 --> 27:28.200
Please come over to the desk.

354
27:28.920 --> 27:30.280
Where is Miss Chayanee?

355
27:31.560 --> 27:32.480
Why?

356
27:37.320 --> 27:39.480
Thank you for taking care

357
27:39.560 --> 27:41.440
of my customers, Hathaya.

358
27:45.560 --> 27:47.440
Mr. Saksit referred you, right?

359
27:47.520 --> 27:50.440
Yes. Mr. Saksit specifically told me to make my reservation with you.

360
27:50.520 --> 27:53.080
He said you have a special VIP promotion.

361
27:53.680 --> 27:56.080
That's right. Please have a seat.

362
28:06.280 --> 28:07.800
That wasn't very nice.

363
28:07.880 --> 28:10.760
It was her customer, but she had someone else do all the work.

364
28:11.480 --> 28:14.400
It's okay. No matter whose customer it is,

365
28:14.480 --> 28:16.720
the development still benefits.

366
28:16.800 --> 28:18.680
Miss Chayanee gets all the credit,

367
28:18.760 --> 28:21.600
and your reservation numbers are already really low this month.

368
28:22.240 --> 28:24.400
There are still several days left, Ploy.

369
28:24.480 --> 28:26.440
I'll work harder.

370
28:33.160 --> 28:34.800
How are this month's reservations?

371
28:46.000 --> 28:47.440
These numbers are very high.

372
28:48.080 --> 28:51.480
I've been doing everything I can. I bring customers to the development,

373
28:51.560 --> 28:55.000
show them the model homes, and persuade them to reserve immediately.

374
28:55.080 --> 28:57.680
I won't let down my reputation as your favorite granddaughter.

375
29:00.040 --> 29:00.920
And yours?

376
29:04.520 --> 29:06.080
Ten houses.

377
29:08.200 --> 29:11.400
You used to have much higher reservation numbers.

378
29:11.480 --> 29:12.960
Looks like you've lost your touch.

379
29:13.800 --> 29:15.520
My numbers aren't high,

380
29:15.600 --> 29:18.200
but every one of my customers is ready to pay cash.

381
29:23.600 --> 29:24.560
And yours?

382
29:25.440 --> 29:27.200
My customers are applying for financing.

383
29:27.720 --> 29:31.520
I already sent their applications to the banks for assessment.

384
29:31.600 --> 29:34.440
Besides, Uncle Saksit referred them,

385
29:34.520 --> 29:36.000
so there shouldn't be any issues.

386
29:37.200 --> 29:38.880
Don't take unnecessary risks.

387
29:39.400 --> 29:42.400
If they don't qualify, they lose time,

388
29:42.920 --> 29:44.480
and we lose opportunities.

389
29:46.080 --> 29:47.120
And also,

390
29:48.000 --> 29:50.720
what promotion did you use to get numbers this high?

391
29:51.840 --> 29:55.160
The usual, free air conditioners and kitchen appliances.

392
29:56.240 --> 29:57.960
The reason the numbers are so high

393
29:58.040 --> 30:00.200
is because Uncle Saksit helped bring in customers.

394
30:00.280 --> 30:02.440
He wanted to help you and me.

395
30:06.720 --> 30:08.920
With the economy slowing down like this,

396
30:11.480 --> 30:15.880
do not use a promotion that refunds their deposit if financing falls through.

397
30:16.520 --> 30:18.040
The risk is far too high.

398
30:19.000 --> 30:20.280
Yes, Grandpa.

399
30:20.800 --> 30:23.000
I definitely won't use that promotion.

400
30:28.880 --> 30:30.960
Chaya, you shouldn't lie to Grandpa.

401
30:33.720 --> 30:35.680
Come on, Hathaya.

402
30:36.920 --> 30:39.920
Low sales don't mean you have to be a tattletale.

403
30:40.000 --> 30:42.000
I'm not tattling.

404
30:42.080 --> 30:44.920
If I wanted to, I would've told Grandpa the truth just now.

405
30:45.680 --> 30:47.080
I didn't lie.

406
30:47.640 --> 30:50.920
I simply didn't mention it because I didn't want Grandpa to worry.

407
30:52.360 --> 30:54.960
I'm confident Mr. Saksit's customers

408
30:55.040 --> 30:57.960
are respectable people who will definitely qualify for financing.

409
30:58.800 --> 31:01.000
And another thing, Hathaya.

410
31:02.120 --> 31:04.280
I've told you before

411
31:04.360 --> 31:06.400
not to lecture me.

412
31:07.120 --> 31:09.520
You should worry about yourself.

413
31:09.600 --> 31:11.680
Your reservation numbers are this low.

414
31:12.360 --> 31:14.680
If you can't handle sales, then give it up

415
31:14.760 --> 31:18.440
and go back to hauling bricks and cement. Go back

416
31:19.040 --> 31:20.360
where you belong.

417
31:23.720 --> 31:24.600
Chayanee.

418
31:25.600 --> 31:26.440
Uncle Saksit.

419
31:29.160 --> 31:33.400
I brought you even more customers who want to buy houses.

420
31:33.480 --> 31:35.600
They're waiting at the model home.

421
31:36.240 --> 31:37.760
Thank you, Uncle.

422
31:37.840 --> 31:39.840
You're so sweet to me.

423
31:39.920 --> 31:43.040
I haven't forgotten what you asked me to do.

424
31:43.920 --> 31:46.640
Then I'll go take care of the customers.

425
31:55.680 --> 31:58.320
When I love someone, I treat them very well.

426
31:59.640 --> 32:02.080
But when I hate someone,

427
32:03.160 --> 32:04.960
I hate them until the day I die.

428
32:17.080 --> 32:18.520
Hello, ma'am.

429
32:20.160 --> 32:21.200
What?

430
32:24.000 --> 32:24.840
Okay.

431
32:34.880 --> 32:38.320
She came in, immediately took charge, and then told me to go home.

432
32:38.400 --> 32:39.920
She said she'd handle Papang herself.

433
32:40.000 --> 32:42.320
Thank you.

434
32:42.400 --> 32:43.520
Where is she now?

435
32:44.600 --> 32:45.640
Inside.

436
32:47.080 --> 32:47.920
Okay.

437
32:55.680 --> 32:57.880
Papang,

438
32:57.960 --> 32:59.640
how much do you love Mommy?

439
32:59.720 --> 33:02.560
I love you more than anyone, Mommy.

440
33:02.640 --> 33:06.080
Mommy loves you more than anyone too.

441
33:06.160 --> 33:08.040
And I love Daddy as much as the whole universe.

442
33:09.040 --> 33:10.000
Hello.

443
33:10.640 --> 33:13.200
Auntie, you're back.

444
33:13.280 --> 33:14.640
Where's Daddy?

445
33:15.240 --> 33:17.400
Daddy has a little more work to do. He'll be home soon.

446
33:17.480 --> 33:19.360
I was worried about you, so I came back first.

447
33:20.440 --> 33:21.360
Okay.

448
33:22.560 --> 33:26.040
Papang, go upstairs and play your game for a while.

449
33:26.120 --> 33:27.400
Okay.

450
33:43.800 --> 33:45.000
You're back.

451
33:45.080 --> 33:48.440
Papang is so happy. He's really glad you're here.

452
33:48.520 --> 33:50.640
Of course. I'm his mother.

453
33:51.760 --> 33:55.040
Naturally, he loves me and wants to be with me,

454
33:55.680 --> 33:57.920
not some outsider who isn't his mother or father.

455
34:02.520 --> 34:04.720
And that "hello" you gave me earlier?

456
34:04.800 --> 34:06.160
Let's change it to "goodbye".

457
34:06.840 --> 34:08.400
Where do you want me to go?

458
34:09.000 --> 34:10.840
We're going to live here together as a family.

459
34:10.920 --> 34:13.120
This house doesn't need you.

460
34:13.679 --> 34:15.960
I'm Ramil's wife.

461
34:16.040 --> 34:18.159
Not some fake wife like you.

462
34:20.560 --> 34:24.360
I know you and Ramil aren't romantically involved.

463
34:26.239 --> 34:28.679
So hurry upstairs, pack your things, and get out.

464
34:31.639 --> 34:32.880
Go.

465
34:33.840 --> 34:36.800
I told you to leave, and you're still here. Shameless.

466
34:38.800 --> 34:40.199
I'm sorry,

467
34:41.120 --> 34:45.159
but you're not the one who gets to decide whether I stay or leave.

468
34:45.239 --> 34:46.880
You don't own this house.

469
34:47.679 --> 34:48.920
You're staying here too.

470
34:49.760 --> 34:51.199
I told you.

471
34:51.719 --> 34:53.960
I'm Ramil's wife.

472
34:54.960 --> 34:57.960
I said go upstairs and pack your clothes. Go.

473
34:59.040 --> 35:00.200
Let go of her.

474
35:06.000 --> 35:07.000
Hathaya.

475
35:08.280 --> 35:09.400
Go get some rest.

476
35:10.680 --> 35:12.320
I'm not finished talking to this woman.

477
35:12.920 --> 35:14.360
Her name is Hathaya.

478
35:14.960 --> 35:16.680
You should address her properly.

479
35:18.240 --> 35:19.400
I need to talk to you.

480
35:20.480 --> 35:21.400
Come here.

481
35:28.320 --> 35:29.480
Let go. You're hurting me.

482
35:31.160 --> 35:32.120
Where have you been?

483
35:32.800 --> 35:35.760
You said you wouldn't be gone long, then you left your son here.

484
35:35.840 --> 35:38.600
Do you have any idea how much he missed you?

485
35:38.680 --> 35:39.960
He even ran away from home.

486
35:40.040 --> 35:41.840
I was working.

487
35:42.720 --> 35:45.440
If I don't work, how am I supposed to support my child?

488
35:45.520 --> 35:47.400
I'm a single mother.

489
35:47.480 --> 35:50.080
Nobody just hands me money for free.

490
35:50.720 --> 35:52.560
And it's not my fault

491
35:53.520 --> 35:56.520
he ran away. It's yours.

492
35:58.600 --> 36:00.360
When he lives with me,

493
36:00.440 --> 36:02.520
he never behaves like this.

494
36:03.320 --> 36:06.720
Maybe that woman upset my son so badly

495
36:06.800 --> 36:08.280
that he ran away.

496
36:08.920 --> 36:09.840
Enough.

497
36:10.640 --> 36:12.520
I'm not wasting time arguing with you.

498
36:13.960 --> 36:16.320
If you want to blame me,

499
36:16.400 --> 36:18.640
fine, I'll take responsibility.

500
36:19.160 --> 36:20.720
But it's good that you're back.

501
36:20.800 --> 36:23.800
I can pack Papang's things, and you can finally take him home.

502
36:23.880 --> 36:25.240
I'm not leaving.

503
36:25.760 --> 36:26.960
My son and I are staying here.

504
36:27.040 --> 36:28.120
What did you say?

505
36:28.200 --> 36:31.880
You know he's been starved for affection.

506
36:31.960 --> 36:34.160
He needs love from both of us.

507
36:34.240 --> 36:35.920
I'm going to live here,

508
36:36.000 --> 36:38.880
so we can be together as a family. Father, mother, and son.

509
36:40.120 --> 36:42.840
But we're only friends. I've never loved you.

510
36:42.920 --> 36:44.880
You may never have loved me,

511
36:45.680 --> 36:47.800
but you shouldn't forget the promise you made.

512
36:52.080 --> 36:52.960
Stop.

513
36:53.480 --> 36:55.960
-Let go of me. -What are you doing? Let go.

514
36:56.040 --> 36:57.400
I said, let me go.

515
36:57.480 --> 37:00.200
-You're pregnant. Stop. -I want to die.

516
37:00.280 --> 37:03.840
Your brother doesn't love me anymore. Let me go.

517
37:06.200 --> 37:09.400
What are you doing? You're having a baby.

518
37:11.080 --> 37:13.160
When the baby is born

519
37:13.240 --> 37:16.240
and asks who the father is, what am I supposed to say?

520
37:17.680 --> 37:19.720
Tell the child I'm the father.

521
37:26.000 --> 37:26.880
Nuch.

522
37:28.680 --> 37:30.080
Please don't hurt yourself.

523
37:32.240 --> 37:34.080
And stay away from Raiwin from now on.

524
37:38.080 --> 37:39.440
I'll claim the baby as mine.

525
37:47.960 --> 37:49.480
You promised me

526
37:49.560 --> 37:51.400
you wouldn't let him suffer.

527
37:51.480 --> 37:53.800
Fine. I'll tell him

528
37:53.880 --> 37:56.840
you're not really his dad and that the two of us don't love each other.

529
37:56.920 --> 37:59.600
Then we'll see what happens

530
37:59.680 --> 38:00.680
when he learns the truth.

531
38:08.240 --> 38:10.800
Daddy. Daddy's home.

532
38:10.880 --> 38:11.920
Papang.

533
38:18.880 --> 38:21.440
What were you and Mommy talking about?

534
38:23.440 --> 38:25.920
Mommy and Daddy were talking about something important.

535
38:27.600 --> 38:30.720
Papang, listen to me.

536
38:31.240 --> 38:33.560
-Mommy and Daddy-- -Love each other very much.

537
38:34.640 --> 38:37.960
Mommy and Daddy

538
38:38.960 --> 38:41.040
-love each other very much. -That's right.

539
38:41.560 --> 38:44.240
Mommy and Daddy love each other very much,

540
38:44.320 --> 38:47.840
and we're going to move in here with Daddy.

541
38:47.920 --> 38:49.000
I'm not going anywhere.

542
38:49.960 --> 38:52.840
Yay. I'm the happiest boy in the world.

543
38:55.960 --> 38:59.120
I'm so happy.

544
38:59.200 --> 39:00.360
Good.

545
39:33.800 --> 39:35.600
Warm soy milk.

546
39:37.600 --> 39:38.840
Thank you.

547
39:40.400 --> 39:41.560
Are you tired?

548
39:48.200 --> 39:49.280
Yeah, I am.

549
39:50.760 --> 39:51.720
But what can I do?

550
39:53.000 --> 39:54.720
Life goes on.

551
39:55.600 --> 39:57.960
Sometimes we don't get to choose.

552
39:59.680 --> 40:00.720
No.

553
40:01.880 --> 40:03.200
I did choose.

554
40:05.360 --> 40:07.240
I chose to protect Papang.

555
40:09.040 --> 40:10.080
So I must face it.

556
40:12.400 --> 40:14.440
I admire what you're doing.

557
40:20.400 --> 40:22.800
And I won't let you fight this alone.

558
40:25.160 --> 40:26.600
I'll help you.

559
40:30.080 --> 40:30.960
And…

560
40:32.960 --> 40:34.240
why would you help me?

561
40:34.960 --> 40:36.880
You helped my family.

562
40:37.720 --> 40:39.520
I want to repay you.

563
40:49.160 --> 40:50.080
Thank you.

564
41:24.520 --> 41:27.440
Your reservation numbers are soaring.

565
41:27.520 --> 41:29.480
My daughter is amazing.

566
41:30.080 --> 41:32.160
Uncle Saksit didn't disappoint us.

567
41:32.240 --> 41:35.280
He promised to help us as much as he could.

568
41:35.360 --> 41:38.080
But what about your workers? Can they finish the houses on time?

569
41:39.160 --> 41:42.240
Don't worry about construction. Pong is good.

570
41:42.320 --> 41:45.480
He's handled hundreds of major projects.

571
41:45.560 --> 41:46.600
He's a professional.

572
41:46.680 --> 41:47.840
Good.

573
41:48.360 --> 41:51.920
I want Grandpa to trust us more than Hathaya.

574
41:52.960 --> 41:54.440
You bring in plenty of customers,

575
41:54.520 --> 41:58.160
and I'll make sure Pong gets the houses built quickly.

576
41:58.800 --> 42:01.440
Before long, Hathaya and Ramil

577
42:01.520 --> 42:03.040
will both be pushed aside.

578
42:03.640 --> 42:06.400
On the next project, I'll convince Father

579
42:06.480 --> 42:08.000
to get rid of them.

580
42:08.080 --> 42:11.320
Come on. Let's go flatter him.

581
42:11.400 --> 42:12.240
Yes.

582
42:15.120 --> 42:16.240
Madam, where are you going?

583
42:16.320 --> 42:18.360
I'm going to see Father. Move.

584
42:19.080 --> 42:20.080
You can't.

585
42:20.760 --> 42:21.600
What is it?

586
42:22.320 --> 42:23.520
So…

587
42:24.040 --> 42:26.560
Pong's workers are gone.

588
42:26.640 --> 42:29.080
Gone? Where did they go?

589
42:29.160 --> 42:30.200
I don't know.

590
42:30.720 --> 42:33.400
All of them are gone.

591
42:36.760 --> 42:38.000
Chamoi,

592
42:38.720 --> 42:40.360
you're such a liar.

593
42:40.440 --> 42:42.320
There are workers everywhere.

594
42:42.920 --> 42:45.320
What were you talking about? Look.

595
42:45.400 --> 42:47.120
Madam,

596
42:47.200 --> 42:50.800
those are Ramil's workers.

597
42:50.880 --> 42:53.440
Pong's workers? Over there.

598
42:56.440 --> 42:58.360
There isn't a single worker.

599
42:58.440 --> 43:01.680
The houses will never get built. Mom, you have to do something.

600
43:02.560 --> 43:06.240
You said your team was professional. How could they just abandon the job?

601
43:08.680 --> 43:11.560
Madam, my team didn't abandon anything.

602
43:11.640 --> 43:13.360
They're just tied up with a bigger project.

603
43:13.440 --> 43:15.440
What do you mean?

604
43:15.520 --> 43:17.680
My grandpa hired them to work here.

605
43:17.760 --> 43:20.400
How can you say they're busy with a bigger job?

606
43:20.480 --> 43:22.320
Miss, you have to understand.

607
43:22.840 --> 43:24.440
Small subcontractors

608
43:24.520 --> 43:27.360
have to keep working so they can pay their crews.

609
43:27.960 --> 43:30.560
But there's work here. Why aren't they doing it?

610
43:30.640 --> 43:34.040
To be frank, madam, the wages here are low.

611
43:34.760 --> 43:36.400
If another place pays more,

612
43:36.480 --> 43:38.440
they're obviously going to work there.

613
43:38.520 --> 43:41.000
Think about it.

614
43:41.080 --> 43:42.600
If it were you, wouldn't you go?

615
43:43.600 --> 43:46.880
But they agreed to this rate before accepting the job.

616
43:46.960 --> 43:49.320
Now somewhere else offers more

617
43:49.400 --> 43:51.920
and they abandon us? That's completely irresponsible.

618
43:52.000 --> 43:54.160
I don't care. You personally guaranteed

619
43:54.240 --> 43:56.160
your team was professional.

620
43:56.240 --> 43:59.600
My daughter and I put our reputations on the line for Father to trust you.

621
44:00.640 --> 44:03.480
Do whatever you have to do. Drag them back here and get them working.

622
44:04.080 --> 44:05.640
I've already done everything I can.

623
44:05.720 --> 44:08.240
I threatened them, begged them.

624
44:08.320 --> 44:12.000
I practically crawled on my knees asking them to come back.

625
44:12.080 --> 44:14.160
So there's no solution?

626
44:15.240 --> 44:16.720
I think

627
44:17.360 --> 44:19.160
there is.

628
44:19.240 --> 44:22.480
What do I have to do to get them back?

629
44:23.120 --> 44:25.560
Right now, there aren't any economic stimulus measures

630
44:25.640 --> 44:29.200
or price controls.

631
44:29.280 --> 44:32.160
Gas, transportation, everything is expensive.

632
44:32.240 --> 44:35.280
Most importantly, the cost of living is high.

633
44:35.360 --> 44:36.800
Wait.

634
44:36.880 --> 44:39.960
What does that have to do with our workers?

635
44:40.040 --> 44:43.320
When everything costs more, wages go up too.

636
44:44.280 --> 44:45.640
You don't understand a thing.

637
44:47.280 --> 44:49.960
Madam, I think you need to increase their pay.

638
44:51.080 --> 44:53.640
Pay more than everyone else. I'm sure they'll come back.

639
44:54.440 --> 44:56.280
But what we're paying is already high enough.

640
44:56.360 --> 44:57.520
Madam,

641
44:58.040 --> 45:00.720
if Mr. Pichai calls Ramil in and has him bring everyone back,

642
45:00.800 --> 45:02.400
he'll take control of the whole project.

643
45:03.080 --> 45:05.120
He'll get all the credit.

644
45:05.200 --> 45:06.920
Think carefully about that.

645
45:08.240 --> 45:10.640
Whatever they want, pay it.

646
45:10.720 --> 45:12.360
But they have to come back tomorrow.

647
45:15.040 --> 45:17.040
Now that's what I call generosity.

648
45:17.640 --> 45:20.120
A true champion of the workers.

649
45:20.200 --> 45:23.400
I'll thank you

650
45:23.480 --> 45:24.760
on their behalf, miss.

651
45:24.840 --> 45:26.320
And thank you too, madam.

652
45:28.200 --> 45:29.520
Servant.

653
45:34.520 --> 45:38.240
Madam, should I call them right now?

654
45:40.360 --> 45:42.840
Madam agreed to raise your pay.

655
45:42.920 --> 45:45.040
Get out of there and come back.

656
45:45.600 --> 45:48.440
Yeah. It's fine.

657
45:48.520 --> 45:49.440
Yeah, all right.

658
45:53.480 --> 45:54.480
Done, madam.

659
46:02.280 --> 46:04.560
You promised to pay them more.

660
46:04.640 --> 46:06.360
Where do we get that extra money?

661
46:06.440 --> 46:09.480
Move money from another budget for now.

662
46:10.760 --> 46:12.960
Did you forget?

663
46:13.040 --> 46:15.040
Grandpa doesn't let me control the accounts anymore.

664
46:16.640 --> 46:19.720
Then use your own money first.

665
46:21.600 --> 46:23.040
Then I'll be broke.

666
46:23.120 --> 46:26.440
Mom, you have to invest.

667
46:26.520 --> 46:29.240
No matter how much money you have to put in, you have to do it.

668
46:29.320 --> 46:31.840
We need to outperform Ramil and Hathaya.

669
46:31.920 --> 46:34.960
What we're really betting on is Grandpa's inheritance.

670
46:35.040 --> 46:36.560
We can afford to lose this much

671
46:36.640 --> 46:38.960
if it means getting everything Grandpa owns.

672
46:44.600 --> 46:46.360
Sorry, madam.

673
46:47.320 --> 46:49.600
But something smells fishy.

674
46:49.680 --> 46:50.760
What?

675
46:51.880 --> 46:53.920
Can you really trust Pong?

676
46:54.000 --> 46:56.320
What if tomorrow or the next day,

677
46:56.400 --> 46:58.320
he asks for another raise?

678
47:00.040 --> 47:01.240
You're right.

679
47:02.280 --> 47:04.640
You don't look smart,

680
47:04.720 --> 47:05.840
but you are.

681
47:06.840 --> 47:07.880
You complimented me.

682
47:10.880 --> 47:13.160
Keep an eye on him.

683
47:13.240 --> 47:14.880
If anything happens, report it to me.

684
47:14.960 --> 47:16.560
It warms my heart that you

685
47:16.640 --> 47:19.520
finally recognize my talent for investigating.

686
47:20.240 --> 47:23.360
Yes. You're number one at sticking your nose where it doesn't belong.

687
47:24.640 --> 47:26.400
Thank you.

688
47:28.720 --> 47:29.840
Was that an insult?

689
47:31.280 --> 47:35.520
Whatever. I'll prove

690
47:35.600 --> 47:39.120
that I investigate. I don't pry.

691
47:41.960 --> 47:43.440
Everything went according to plan.

692
47:43.960 --> 47:45.320
I told you guys to stop working,

693
47:46.800 --> 47:48.960
and she immediately raised the wages.

694
47:52.480 --> 47:54.760
Come early tomorrow. Bring all your stuff.

695
47:55.400 --> 47:57.640
I'll find another excuse to get you another raise.

696
47:59.080 --> 48:00.880
Okay. That's the plan. See you tomorrow.

697
48:14.880 --> 48:17.480
He was just here. Where did he go?

698
48:28.080 --> 48:29.280
Looking for someone, Auntie?

699
48:29.360 --> 48:31.840
No. I'm not looking for anyone.

700
48:31.920 --> 48:34.440
I was just taking a walk.

701
48:34.960 --> 48:37.400
I was born

702
48:37.480 --> 48:39.840
at a construction site, you know.

703
48:39.920 --> 48:43.360
I love the smell of cement and dirt.

704
48:45.240 --> 48:48.600
It's so refreshing. Reminds me

705
48:49.480 --> 48:51.520
of my mom and dad.

706
48:52.720 --> 48:54.560
You miss your mom and dad that much?

707
48:55.680 --> 48:57.240
Yeah. A lot.

708
49:02.280 --> 49:03.440
Then…

709
49:05.520 --> 49:06.440
how about…

710
49:08.640 --> 49:12.040
I take you to see them? I'll help you out.

711
49:13.320 --> 49:15.600
No. That's okay.

712
49:15.680 --> 49:17.680
I'm not ready to go yet.

713
49:18.920 --> 49:20.080
You sure?

714
49:20.160 --> 49:21.360
Yes.

715
49:22.120 --> 49:24.320
I think I'll

716
49:24.840 --> 49:27.880
take my walk over there instead. Something about this area

717
49:28.400 --> 49:30.040
suddenly doesn't feel very healthy.

718
49:31.560 --> 49:33.720
It's a construction site, Auntie.

719
49:33.800 --> 49:35.040
Not a place for a stroll.

720
49:35.120 --> 49:37.520
Right. Construction site.

721
49:39.800 --> 49:41.120
Keep prying into my business

722
49:42.400 --> 49:44.240
and you're going to die badly, you hag.

723
49:47.360 --> 49:50.360
Madam, Ramil's real wife is here.

724
49:50.440 --> 49:51.960
She's been going around telling everyone

725
49:52.040 --> 49:54.160
she's Ramil's wife.

726
49:54.240 --> 49:56.000
Are you still angry with me

727
49:56.080 --> 49:59.120
because I like Raiwin, the same man you like?

728
49:59.200 --> 50:02.200
Raiwin wasn't interested in you, so you went back to Ramil.

729
50:02.280 --> 50:03.240
You really are something.

730
50:03.320 --> 50:05.280
‎NEXT EPISODE

731
50:05.360 --> 50:07.680
Mom, I hate her.

732
50:08.680 --> 50:10.720
-Grandpa! -Sir!

733
52:06.840 --> 52:08.840
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
